Hi folks

Thank you for all the work on the kernel.  Much appreciated.

Kernel Version : 2.6.11.5 (config attached)

Machine : Dell Latitude LS Laptop (specs attached)

Problem Summary : On modprobing the snd_nm256 driver, I experience an
instantaneous and irretrievable system freeze.

Problem Report : The laptop runs Mandrake 10.1.  I have compiled a fresh
kernel from the 2.6.11.5 source with the attached config (mainly to get
my iPod working!!).  The laptop has a NeoMagic 256AV PCI sound system.
I compiled the snd_nm256 ALSA driver as a module.  When I attempt to
modprobe the driver the entire machine freezes irretrievably.  It no
longer responds to any keystrokes (including magic sysreq).  There are
no kernel messages or logged errors of any kind.  The only way to
retrieve the system is to do a hard reboot.

Using modprobe -v does show that the required supporting modules are
inserted but the machine actually freezes when it gets to the snd_nm256
module.  I cannot trap this output (short of a digital photo) because
the machine becomes unresponsive.

I have successfully modprobed the driver once and the sound system
seemed to operate correctly.  However I failed to get any statistics on
the system state at that time.  I can reproduce the problem but do not
know how to obtain any further log / debug output.  Neither do I know
what information might be useful if I can successfully modprobe the
driver again.

The stock kernel from the Mandrake 10.1 install (2.6.8.1-12mdk) does not
exhibit this problem.

Keywords : Kernel, Drivers, Sound, PCI, Neomagic, snd_nm256


Attachments :
ver_linux.output.txt - output of the ver_linux script
config	- the .config file used to compile the kernel
machine.specs.txt - the contents of various /proc files & lspci output


Please contact me if there is any more information you need to look at this.

Cheers

